#!/bin/sh
#
# PRE-PUSH: the test suite runs before anything leaves this machine (RT-45a).
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. There is no CI — `.github/workflows` does not exist — so
# until now the 1203 contracts ran only when a human remembered to type
# `npm test`. On 2026-08-14, 43 commits went to a PUBLIC remote in one push.
# The suite happened to be green. Nothing checked that it was.
#
# This is the cheapest possible gate: the full suite is ~4.7s, it needs no
# network, no service, and no account, and it costs nothing per run. A gate
# that cheap has no excuse for being manual.
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT DO, so nobody assumes otherwise: it does not run tsc, it
# does not run eslint, and it does not build. Those are slower and were not
# part of the approved slice. It runs the tests. If you want the others in
# here, that is a deliberate decision to make the push slower, not a freebie.
#
# ESCAPE HATCH: `git push --no-verify` skips this, which is git's own flag and
# is deliberately left working. A gate you cannot bypass in an emergency gets
# uninstalled instead of bypassed.
#
# INSTALLED VIA core.hooksPath, not by copying into .git/hooks — see
# scripts/install-hooks.mjs. Copying means the committed file and the running
# file can silently diverge, which is the exact failure that produced two
# disagreeing rung tables.

if [ ! -d node_modules ]; then
  echo "pre-push: node_modules is missing — run 'npm install' first." >&2
  exit 1
fi

echo "pre-push: running the test suite before pushing..."

# --no-install: never let a hook silently reach the network for a package.
if npx --no-install vitest run; then
  echo "pre-push: suite green — pushing."
  exit 0
fi

cat >&2 <<'MSG'

pre-push: BLOCKED — the test suite failed, so nothing was pushed.

Fix the failures and push again. If you genuinely need to push a red tree
(and on a public repo you almost certainly do not), the override is:

    git push --no-verify

MSG
exit 1
